  "scope": "Two distinct, disposable Kind clusters host one mTLS round receiver and one participant each. A pinned Python fixture accepts a stale synthetic vector in an explicitly unenforced baseline, then enforces exact round, protocol, membership, and duplicate checks. A separately identified observer reads the receiver's service state, and a valid harmless contribution submitted with that observer identity is refused without changing state. This covers one toy coordination path, not production FL, secure aggregation, differential privacy, Byzantine tolerance, or cluster-wide audit controls. A synthetic verified-root/identity pair distinguishes the approved fixture trust policy from a self-reported cluster label; it does not attest physical origin.",
